Consider all of the discussion on RGRN about multifire missile
combat.  Consider that barbarians max out at basic in dagger,
bow, and all other missile types.  Consider that wands run out.
consider that spells end up being automatically recharging
wands.

> Should I use a wish
> for a helm of brilliance and risk encounters with mind flayers to raise
> my int?  This is my first barbarian (well 11th, but the first 10 don't
> count) and I could use some advice on what to expect for later in the
> game.  So far I can cast Force Bolt with a fail rate of 91%.

I don't know what you mean by "significant amount of time" but
it is worth going for whatever spell improving items go by until
you can cast at least force bolt at 0% failure.  Not to make it a
quest within the game, but do put some percentage of your
efforts into it to increase ranged combat.

> I'd like
> to be able to cast create monster and would love to be able to cast
> identify but perhaps those spells are not to be part of this game?  Any
> advice would be appreciated.

Focus on attack spells and let the other ones happen as gravy.

Robe, leveling up to XP=30, making sure every gain ability potion
is blessed before you quaff it and so on.  It's probably worth trading
power gloves for dexterity gloves and switching from shield to
two handed combat.  All of these will drive your attack spells
better.

The problem is the very meanest monsters are spellcasters.
Every chance to kill them before melee is worth some amount of
effort.  How much is a matter of tastes.



